## Why This Is Asked
Tests privacy-preserving on-device ML, multimodal fusion, and efficient latency. Evaluates understanding of FL/DP, quantization, and on-device retrieval with drift handling.

## Key Concepts
- On-device inference and latency budgeting
- Multimodal embedding fusion
- Federated learning with secure aggregation and differential privacy
- Approximate nearest neighbors for retrieval

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo on-device inference sketch
function inference(text, image) {
  const t = textEncoder.encode(text);
  const i = imageEncoder.encode(image);
  const z = fuse(t, i);
  return topK(z, 5);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor and respond to drift in user preferences?
- How would you handle new modalities or cold-start users without central data access?

## Why This Is Asked
Real-world fintech ML requires low-latency scoring, robust drift handling, and strict auditing. The two-tier approach balances speed and accuracy, while feature stores and drift detectors address production reliability. The privacy angle forces region-aware controls and compliant data flows.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time inference with online/offline learning
- Streaming feature stores and windowing
- Calibration and drift detection
- Auditing and privacy/compliance constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: online score update using SGD
let w = initWeights();
for (event of stream) {
  let x = extractFeatures(event); // windowed features
  let p = sigmoid(dot(w, x));
  updateWeights(w, x, label, p);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate latency under peak load across regions?
- What drift-detection metrics would you track and how would you trigger retraining?

## Why This Is Asked

This tests practical transfer learning on small data, calibration awareness, and a simple data-collection loop.

## Key Concepts

- Transfer learning with lightweight nets
- Data augmentation for small datasets
- Probability calibration (temperature scaling)
- Active/incremental labeling
- Evaluation: accuracy and calibration metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: load pretrained MobileNetV2, replace head, train on 2k images
const model = loadPretrained('MobileNetV2');
model.detachHead();
model.addHead(5);
model.freezeLayers(['conv1','conv2']);
model.compile({lr: 1e-4, loss: 'categoricalCrossentropy', optimizer:'adam'});
model.fit(dataset, {epochs: 5, augment: true});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this with a simple active-learning loop?
- What failure modes could undermine calibration on unseen classes?

## Why This Is Asked

